 **Doctrine, enforced in the tools, not just stated here:** we measure, never
-certify. Verdicts are three-state — VALID / INVALID (with the reason) /
-UNCHECKABLE — never two-state. An unmeasured axis is a first-class answer, not
+certify. Cryptographic `verify_card` verdicts are three-state — VALID /
+INVALID (with the reason) / UNCHECKABLE. Retrieval results use separate,
+explicitly unverified states. An unmeasured axis is a first-class answer, not
